  <data name="textMain.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Financially Responsible Person: This is the person who signed financial responsibility with your office. The
financially responsible person is not automatically the person who holds the insurance. The signature should not
be more than one year old from when services were provided. Do not send a minor child to collections.

Collection Letter: Trojan will send the consumer one collection letter (diplomatic or firm). The consumer is
instructed to pay your office directly. Trojan will report the account to the credit bureaus after 30 days if no
payment has been paid.

Skip: Use this option when statements are being returned without a forwarding address. A Tracker Report will
be mailed to your office. If a new address is located, contact Trojan within 30 days and we will send a diplomatic
or firm collection letter at no additional cost. If a new address is not found the consumer will still be reported to
the credit bureaus.

Delinquency Date: If no payments have been made, the delinquency date is 30 days after the last treatment
was provided. If a partial payment has been made, the delinquency date is 30 days after the last payment.
Balance: Include all past due charges. You may add finance charges and collection costs as long as the financial
responsibility consent includes these fees.

Collection Services Password: This password is two letters followed by four digits. It was assigned to your
office when you signed up for Trojan's Collection Services.

Questions: Contact Trojan's Collection Services Department at 800-248-2964. We're open Monday through
Thursday from 6:00 am to 5:00 pm PST and Friday from 6:00 am to 4:00 pm PST.
</value>
